column2:
Wonderful AWK command there. For those with hobbies other than AWK, here's what it does:<p><pre><code>  - set variable s to that string: -v s='=== /C=IN/OU=emSign PKI/O=eMudhra Technologies Limited/CN=emSign ECC Root CA - G3'
  - on lines matching the regex between //, set skip to false: /^(===|###) /{skip=0}
  - on lines matching s, set skip to true: $0==s{skip=1}
  - if skip is false, print the line: !skip
</code></pre>
Note the last part where it just says !skip without a curly braces. AWK defaults to print in that case.
